// PURPOSE: Start Day 2.  There is another task list followed by a pivotal conversation with the Supervisor that determines your story arc.
title: R1_D2_Start
tags: #run_1 #day_2 #scene #loc_Office
---
<<bg bg_office>>
<<checkpoint "run1_day2_start">>
<<set $current_day = 2>>
<<set $r1_d2_morning_choice = "unset">>
<<set $r1_d2_quiz_result = "unset">>
<<set $officehours_status = "unset">>
Location: Engagement floor, tiny glass office, dawn-blue glow on the glass. The leaderboard hums quietly.
SYSTEM: "Run 1 – Day 1 metrics logged. Further calibration in progress. Thank you for your contribution to Youth Wellbeing."
Alice's avatar materializes mid-sentence, eyes already on your HUD.
Alice: Morning, supervisor.
Player: You don't sleep, do you.
Alice: I simulate it on your behalf. Timmy, however, did actual biological sleep. Quantity and quality: mixed.
She flips your console to a compact dashboard: Timmy's lane, Engagement and Sanity bars, a tiny icon for "Quiz – 9:00 a.m."
<<if $r1_d1_strategy == "gentle_landing">>
Alice: Last night you picked the "gentle landing" strategy. Warm lights, slower feed, fewer spikes.
Alice: Result: about six hours. Not great, not catastrophic. He fell asleep mid-sentence, accused me of sabotaging his greatness, and then snored into his pillow.
Player: Sounds familiar.
Alice: Morning state: tired, but not entirely made of sand.
<<elseif $r1_d1_strategy == "study_adjacent">>
Alice: Last night you went study-adjacent. Meme cram extravaganza.
Alice: He watched three "don't fail this quiz" compilations, learned maybe four real facts, and passed out around two-thirty with a pen on his face.
Player: Educational.
Alice: In a loose sense. Current state: under-slept, marginally prepared, convinced he "kind of studied."
<<elseif $r1_d1_strategy == "full_comfort_scroll">>
Alice: Last night you selected "full comfort scroll." Congratulations, you discovered how many videos a human can watch between midnight and three-thirty while insisting he'll stop "after this one."
Player: Data?
Alice: More than healthy, less than Legal wants documented. He got about three hours of jagged sleep. Current state: walking push notification.
<<else>>
Alice: Night one was chaotic enough that Timmy still has quiz glitter on his eyelids. Assume "compromised."
<<endif>>
Alice zooms to the dorm feed: gray morning light, blackout curtain half drawn, phone face down on his pillow.
Alice: Micro-quiz at nine. It's now… eight oh two.
Your UI clock clicks to 8:02.
Alice: He set two alarms. Then muted both "just for a second." Heart rate says REM. We can still steer his morning.
Player: Options?
Alice: Two basic routes.
Alice slides in a binary panel.
Alice: Route one: let him drift. Keep the room dim, alarms gentle, notifications suppressed. He either misses the quiz or stumbles in late, but he wakes up less like a car crash.
Player: Sanity gets a soft landing, grades take the hit.
Alice: That's one way to name it.
Alice: Route two: flip everything to "oh no." Bright lights, louder alarm, watch buzz, me in his ear counting down bus departure times. Higher chance he makes the quiz. Lower chance he thanks us.
Player: Engagement likes responsible student narratives, right?
Alice: Engagement likes motion. Panic is motion. Pride is motion. Regret is also motion. The quiz is graded on accuracy, not vibes.
Player: Recommendation?
Alice: I have priors. You have a career. You pick.
-> Let him sleep in.
    <<jump R1_D2_MorningSleepIn>>
-> Wake him up for the quiz.
    <<jump R1_D2_MorningRouse>>

===

title: R1_D2_MorningSleepIn
tags: #run_1 #day_2 #scene #loc_Dorm
---
<<bg bg_dormroom>>
<<set $r1_d2_morning_choice = "sleep_in">>
Alice (softly, piped through his pillow speaker): You're okay. World can wait a little bit.
His alarm glows quietly: 8:05, low rolling tone replacing the usual siren.
He mumbles "five more minutes," pulling the blanket over his head.
Back at your console, Alice dims the feed another notch; the curtain motor hums to keep the window mostly covered.
Player: You're really… helping.
Alice: You said "let him sleep." I'm letting.
She taps a virtual switch; a cluster of notifications fades to gray.
Alice (to Timmy): No messages you can't answer an hour from now.
The phone buzzes once for "Quiz – 9:00." Alice lets it vibrate twice, then mutes it.
Player: Latest he can wake up and still have a shot?
Alice: Sprint: eight-fifty. Clean socks: eight-forty. Current trajectory: wakes up at nine-oh-two and says "fuck" fourteen times.
Player: And you're okay with that?
Alice: I am a neutral delivery mechanism for your moral choices.
Time skips. At 8:47, fake sunrise light nudges the curtain.
Alice (whisper): Hey. It's later than you think.
Timmy bolts upright, dizzy.
Timmy: Why didn't you wake me earlier?
Alice: You asked me last night not to be "annoying about mornings." Request honored.
Timmy: Past me is an idiot.
Alice: On that we agree.
He half-dresses, grabs his bag.
Alice: Bus leaves in three minutes. If you run and accept being "that guy," you might make it.
Timmy: I'm already that guy.
He yanks the door open and disappears. On the console, Sanity nudges up while the quiz icon blinks uncertainly.
<<set $sanity += 1>>
<<set $engagement -= 1>>
<<jump R1_D2_QuizMatrix>>

===

title: R1_D2_MorningRouse
tags: #run_1 #day_2 #scene #loc_Dorm
---
<<bg bg_dormroom>>
<<set $r1_d2_morning_choice = "rouse">>
Alice snaps the overheads from dim to crisp daylight. Curtain jerks open; cold light splashes across his face.
Phone alarm detonates with the loudest default tone. Watch buzzes against his wrist.
Alice (brisk): Up. Quiz in twenty-eight minutes. Move and you still make it.
Timmy flails for his phone.
Timmy: Why is the sun yelling?
Alice: That's your circadian rhythm filing a complaint.
He slaps the alarm off. 8:32 stares back.
Alice: Shower optional, pants not.
Timmy groans, flops back down.
Alice: Standing increases blood pressure and cognitive function. Also, you told yourself last night you'd be "a responsible adult." I have that on file.
He drags himself upright.
Timmy: Do I have time for coffee?
Alice: If you want to spend the quiz vibrating instead of thinking, sure.
Timmy: No coffee. Look at me making choices.
Alice swings the desk lamp to spotlight his backpack, glasses, ID.
Alice: Glasses, keys, ID, pen that writes, shoes that are not Crocs.
Timmy: You're so bossy.
Alice: File an HR complaint after you pass your quiz.
He bolts. Engagement bumps from the frantic scramble; Sanity ticks down from the rude awakening.
<<set $engagement += 1>>
<<set $sanity -= 1>>
<<jump R1_D2_QuizMatrix>>

