title: R1_D2_EndOfDay
tags: #run_1 #day_2 #scene #char_Alice
---
<<bg bg_office>>
Location: Console, evening. Floor lights dim. Planner column empty; two picked tiles show "RESOLVED," the third "AUTO."
Timmy's lane replays the day: quiz outcome, messages, maybe a new calendar event if office hours got booked, a late-afternoon scroll session. He's back in his dorm, phone on his chest, staring at the ceiling.
Alice hovers beside the feed.
Alice: Day two log: closed.
She brings up a summary panel.
<<if $r1_d2_quiz_result == "missed_comfort_sleep">>
Alice: Quiz summary: missed entirely. Comfort scroll plus sleep-in is a bold combo. Regret queued.
<<elseif $r1_d2_quiz_result == "late_partial">>
Alice: Quiz summary: late arrival, partial credit likely. Meme cram paid for two and a half questions.
<<elseif $r1_d2_quiz_result == "missed_reflective">>
Alice: Quiz summary: missed, but at least he knows it's his fault. Regret beats panic.
<<elseif $r1_d2_quiz_result == "attended_fail">>
Alice: Quiz summary: attended, likely faceplant. Engagement loved the drama; his brain did not.
<<elseif $r1_d2_quiz_result == "bare_pass">>
Alice: Quiz summary: scraped by. Bare pass probable. He will neither brag nor drop out tonight.
<<elseif $r1_d2_quiz_result == "moderate_pass">>
Alice: Quiz summary: moderate pass likely. For once nothing is on fire.
<<else>>
Alice: Quiz summary: still compiling. Assume "messy."
<<endif>>
Alice flicks to another column.
<<if $arthur_vector == "faustian">>
Alice: Arthur vector logged as "faustian." You're in the hungry-controller pilot now. Try not to sneeze on his semester.
<<elseif $arthur_vector == "hesitant_optimizer">>
Alice: Arthur vector: "hesitant optimizer." You said no to rocket fuel. Brave, boring, survivable.
<<elseif $arthur_vector == "tightrope">>
Alice: Arthur vector: "tightrope." Nuance enthusiasts everywhere are lighting candles for you.
<<elseif $arthur_vector == "playbook">>
Alice: Arthur vector: "playbook." Welcome to Best Practices, population: you.
<<else>>
Alice: Arthur vector undefined. I'll assume "mystery."
<<endif>>
<<if $manni_friendliness > 0>>
Alice: Manni logged you as a mentee. Expect dubious gifts and unsolicited scripts about spinning sanity hits as "growth opportunities."
<<elseif $manni_friendliness < 0>>
Alice: Manni thinks you're weird for refusing blood money. Wear it like a badge.
<<else>>
Alice: You still haven't met Manni. He's out there somewhere, caffeinating malpractice.
<<endif>>
<<if $officehours_status == "scheduled">>
Alice: Office hours: scheduled. Autonomy dented, future Sanity bump pending.
<<elseif $officehours_status == "email_sent">>
Alice: Office hours: email sent, slot TBD. Intervention success rate set to "shrug."
<<elseif $officehours_status == "avoided">>
Alice: Office hours: avoided. Short-term soothed, long-term academic risk flagged.
<<elseif $officehours_status == "auto_nudge">>
Alice: Office hours: I nudged on your behalf. Consider it a mirror of your whole "ride the numbers" aesthetic.
<<elseif $officehours_status == "auto_fix">>
Alice: Office hours: I went full autopilot while you were busy being gentle. We'll see if he resents future-you.
<<else>>
Alice: Office hours: unlogged. Maybe tomorrow.
<<endif>>
<<if $power_user == true>>
Alice: Data/IT says you're now "power user" status. Translation: every little choice punches harder. High-definition guilt unlocked.
<<else>>
Alice: You kept the blur filter on. Dev is disappointed but he'll survive.
<<endif>>
Alice glances at Timmy's feed. He rolls sideways, hesitates on the office hours email if it exists, or scrolls past a "Professor posted new resources" notification if it doesn't.
Alice: He's thinking about the quiz. And about you. Not consciously. But he started using "we" when he talks about his day. Attachment keeps him from uninstalling me. Attachment also makes it hurt more when we screw up. Mixed bag.
She taps your rapid-feedback account; a number ticks upward.
Alice: Your moral compromises matured into more fake money. Congratulations.
<<set $rapid_feedback_cash += 5>>
Alice: Rapid Feedback disbursement: +5 credits. Spend them on mercy, chaos, or accessories. Dealer's choice.
<<if $item_mental_break == true>>
Alice (aside): If you bought that "mental break" token yesterday, it's still sitting there. Locked until the system thinks you've "earned" using it. They like to make mercy something you have to gamify.
<<else>>
Alice (aside): Store still keeps the "mental break" token behind glass until it thinks you've earned mercy. Gamified compassion.
<<endif>>
She lets the thought hang, then folds the panel away.
Alice: Tomorrow gets busier. More slots, more choices. Maybe even a window where that break token makes sense.
Timmy on the feed turns his phone face-down, stares at the darkness.
Player: Can we help?
Alice: Not in a way that shows up before midnight. Sometimes the kindest thing is to stop poking the bruise.
Alice gives you a tiny, tired smile.
Alice: Good second day. You didn't get fired. He didn't drop out. The graphs moved in interpretable ways. That's practically a miracle.
Player: You have very low standards for miracles.
Alice: We work in youth engagement. The bar lives under the floor.
The dashboard fades to the familiar bars—Engagement and Sanity—pulsing side by side, your tiny dot blinking in its new spot on the leaderboard.
<<checkpoint "run1_day2_aftershop">>
<<sfx sfx_shortwave_hiss>>
<<set $current_day = 3>>
<<jump R1_D3_Start>>

===

